%S A395686 3,95,105,114,183,437,609,682,827,902,1090,1153,1215,1378
%N A395686 Numbers k such that Lucas(k) is a Smith number.
%C A395686 a(15) >= 1423. - _Michael S. Branicky_, Aug 05 2026
%D A395686 Shyam Sunder Gupta, Smith Numbers, Exploring the Beauty of Fascinating Numbers, Springer (2025) Ch. 4, 127-157.
%H A395686 factordb.com, <a href="https://factordb.com/index.php?query=Lucas%281423%29">Status of Lucas(1423)</a>,
%H A395686 B. Kelly, <a href="https://mersennus.net/fibonacci/l1000.txt">Factorization of L_n, n = 0..1000</a>.
%e A395686 a(2) = 95 because L(95) = 71420983074726546239 = 11*191*9349*41611*87382901.
%e A395686 The decimal digit sum of L(95) is 89, while digit_sum(11*191*9349*41611*87382901) = 2 + 11 + 25 + 13 + 38 = 89.
%Y A395686 Cf. A000032 (Lucas numbers), A006753 (Smith numbers).
